━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Session
    is Usable'Void

` One type pass over a program. A pass of a parallel type pass holds what the passes share
` (`shared`), has offered them the instances its typing queued before `offered`, and keeps in
` `local` those of them only it can intern, to type itself. It has published those of
` `Instances.settled` before `shared-settled`, whose errors settled after their bodies ended. The
` modules whose mains or whose functions it was seeded with (`seeded-modules`,
` `seeded-functions`) seed it again where it starts over (`restart`).

+ program Program
+ bindings Bindings
+ binder Binder
+ types Types
+ relations Relations
+ scratch TypingScratch
+ instances Instances
+ facts Facts
+ errors ErrorSets
+ panics Panics
+ shared SharedTyping?
+ offered Size
+ shared-settled Size
+ local [InstanceId]
+ seeded-modules [ModuleId]
+ seeded-functions [Bool]
+ unreached-modules [ModuleId]
+ typed-amid-errors [Bool]
_ arena Arena
_ facts-arena Arena
_ typing-released Bool
_ released Bool

────────────────────
+ This
    - program Program

.. bindings = Bindings()
.. scratch = TypingScratch()
.. types = bound-types(program, scratch)
.. binder = Binder(bindings, program, types.builtin-classes)
.. relations = Relations(types)
.. instances = Instances(arena, types)
.. facts = Facts(facts-arena, instances)
.. errors = ErrorSets(facts-arena, types, relations, instances, facts, program)
.. panics = Panics(types, program, instances, facts)

────────────────────
+ do note-seed
    - module ModuleId
    - functions Bool

seeded-modules += module
seeded-functions += functions

────────────────────
+ do retarget
    - next Program

program = next
binder.retarget(next)
types.program = next
relations.program = next
panics.program = next
errors.retarget(next)
scratch.idle.clear()

────────────────────
+ do restart

` Drops everything typed so far for a pass that knows from the start every property the
` pass so far found tracked (`Panics.seed`).
. tracked = panics.tracked-keys()
. traces-lint = facts.traces-lint
release()
released = false
typing-released = false
arena = Arena()
facts-arena = Arena()
scratch = TypingScratch()
bindings = Bindings()
types = bound-types(program, scratch)
binder = Binder(bindings, program, types.builtin-classes)
relations = Relations(types)
instances = Instances(arena, types)
facts = Facts(facts-arena, instances)
facts.traces-lint = traces-lint
errors = ErrorSets(facts-arena, types, relations, instances, facts, program)
panics = Panics(types, program, instances, facts)
panics.seed(tracked)
offered = 0
local.clear()

────────────────────
+ begin-using

this

────────────────────
+ do end-using

release()

────────────────────
+ do seal

` Seals the type store over every type the instances typed and the facts still name, and the
` instance table with it, so nothing that runs after typing can intern or complete a type or
` schedule an instance. An instance that raises errors is first given the type it returns, which
` emission can no longer make, and so is a member a union forwards whose cases let errors out,
` and a local rule of one, for the function the reference may make of the rule, an action
` of one the reference runs in a function of its own, and a pattern of one given to a rule
` that calls a local rule, with the rule it is given to.
for position in 0 .. < instances.signatures.length
    . signature = instances.signatures[position]
    if signature.errors.count == 0 || signature.returns == invalid-type
        continue
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
        scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
    . value = if signature.returns == no-type then types.void-type else signature.returns
    instances.set-result(position as InstanceId, result-type(types, value, mark))
for position in 0 .. < facts.local-rules.length
    . row = facts.local-rules[position]
    . signature = instances.signatures[row.instance]
    if signature.errors.count != 0 && row.answer != no-type && row.answer != invalid-type
        . mark = scratch.types.mark
        for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
            scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
        facts.local-rules[position].result = result-type(types, row.answer, mark)
        if row.adapted != no-type
            . relayed = scratch.types.mark
            for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
                scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
            facts.local-rules[position].relayed = result-type(types, row.adapted, relayed)
for position in 0 .. < facts.outlined.length
    . row = facts.outlined[position]
    . signature = instances.signatures[row.instance]
    . value = facts.node-type(row.instance, row.arm)
    if signature.errors.count != 0 && value != no-type && value != invalid-type
        . mark = scratch.types.mark
        for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
            scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
        facts.outlined[position].result = result-type(types, value, mark)
. raised = false
for position in 0 .. < facts.pattern-arguments.length
    . row = facts.pattern-arguments[position]
    . signature = instances.signatures[row.instance]
    if row.local != 0 && signature.errors.count != 0 && answered
        . mark = scratch.types.mark
        for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
            scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
        facts.pattern-arguments[position].raised = result-type(types, row.answer, mark)
        raised = true
    .. answered = row.answer != no-type && row.answer != invalid-type
if raised
    note-raising-rules()
for position in 0 .. < facts.forwards.length
    settle-forward(position)
for position in 0 .. < instances.rows.length
    . row = instances.rows[position]
    if row.state == .instance-unstarted
        continue
    . signature = instances.signatures[position]
    types.reach(row.self-type)
    types.reach(row.yields)
    types.reach(signature.returns)
    types.reach(signature.declared-returns)
    types.reach(signature.result)
    for offset in signature.args.start - signature.param-count .. < signature.args.start + signature.args.count
        types.reach(instances.signature-types[offset])
    for offset in signature.errors.start .. < signature.errors.start + signature.errors.count
        types.reach(instances.signature-types[offset])
    for offset in row.step-errors.start .. < row.step-errors.start + row.step-errors.count
        types.reach(instances.signature-types[offset])
    if row.slot-start != U32.max
        for offset in row.slot-start .. < row.slot-start + row.slot-count
            types.reach(facts.slot-types[offset])
    if row.node-start != U32.max
        for offset in row.node-start .. < row.node-start + row.subtree.count
            types.reach(facts.node-types[offset])
for held in facts.loose-types
    types.reach(held.type)
for held in facts.answer-types
    types.reach(held.type)
for row in facts.pattern-arguments
    types.reach(row.result)
    types.reach(row.answer)
    types.reach(row.stream)
    types.reach(row.buffer)
    types.reach(row.helper)
    types.reach(row.raised)
for row in facts.raising-rules
    types.reach(row.given)
    types.reach(row.result)
for row in facts.local-rules
    types.reach(row.answer)
    types.reach(row.result)
    types.reach(row.stream)
    types.reach(row.buffer)
    types.reach(row.adapted)
    types.reach(row.relayed)
for row in facts.outlined
    types.reach(row.result)
for forward in facts.forwards
    types.reach(forward.result)
for fact in facts.conversions
    types.reach(fact.from)
    types.reach(fact.to)
for fact in facts.conversion-parts
    types.reach(fact.from)
    types.reach(fact.to)
for fact in facts.pairs
    types.reach(fact.from)
    types.reach(fact.to)
    types.reach(fact.unified)
for type in facts.equalities
    types.reach(type)
for type in facts.carried
    types.reach(type)
for fact in facts.unwrapped
    types.reach(fact.type)
for fact in facts.relations
    types.reach(fact.from)
    types.reach(fact.to)
for fact in facts.forces
    types.reach(fact.operand)
    types.reach(fact.result)
for fact in facts.declared-values
    types.reach(fact.declared)
    types.reach(fact.found)
for fact in facts.context-casts
    types.reach(fact.target)
for fact in facts.case-owners
    types.reach(fact.owner)
for table in facts.witness-tables
    types.reach(table.value)
    types.reach(table.interface)
for table in facts.dynamic-witnesses
    types.reach(table.value)
    types.reach(table.interface)
for func in facts.witness-funcs
    types.reach(func.interface)
for call in facts.witness-calls
    types.reach(call.interface)
for diagnostic in facts.diagnostics
    types.reach(diagnostic.from)
    types.reach(diagnostic.to)
for type in facts.diagnostic-mentions
    types.reach(type)
for material in facts.materials
    types.reach(material.type)
    types.reach(material.interface)
for body in facts.rollback-bodies
    types.reach(body.held)
    types.reach(body.kept)
for body in facts.storage-bodies
    types.reach(body.context)
for trigger in facts.markup-triggers
    types.reach(trigger.target)
    types.reach(trigger.found)
    types.reach(trigger.host)
    types.reach(trigger.changes)
types.seal()
instances.seal()

────────────────────
_ do note-raising-rules

` Records, for each call of a rule that gives it a pattern whose function may raise errors,
` what the function of the rule made for such a pattern returns: the rule's answer or one of
` the errors the pattern's function returns. A rule that raises errors of its own has none.
for fact in facts.calls
    if fact.callee == no-instance || fact.instance == instances.dead || raises
        continue
    .. raises = instances.signatures[fact.callee].errors.count != 0
    . tree = program.modules[instances.rows[fact.instance].module].tree
    do match? tree.nodes[fact.syntax]
        | .node-stream-call(call)
            for offset in 0 .. < call.args.count
                . argument = tree.children[call.args.start + offset]
                . expression = argument
                do match? tree.nodes[argument]
                    | .node-argument(named)
                        expression = named.expr
                . given = raised-pattern(fact.instance, expression)
                if given != no-type
                    note-raising-rule(fact.callee, fact.instance, given)

────────────────────
_ do raised-pattern TypeId
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` What the function made of a pattern an instance gives a rule returns where it may raise
` errors, or none.
for row in facts.pattern-arguments
    if row.instance == instance && row.syntax == syntax
        = row.raised
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do note-raising-rule
    - callee InstanceId
    - caller InstanceId
    - given TypeId

` Records what a rule given a pattern whose function returns `given` returns, once, and
` what the function of each of its local rules does.
for row in facts.raising-rules
    if row.instance == callee && row.given == given
        =
. returns = instances.signatures[callee].returns
if returns == no-type || returns == invalid-type
    =
. signature = instances.signatures[caller]
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
    scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
facts.raising-rules.append(RaisingRule(callee, given, result-type(types, returns, mark)))
for position in 0 .. < facts.local-rules.length
    . local = facts.local-rules[position]
    if local.instance != callee || local.answer == no-type || local.answer == invalid-type
        continue
    . held = scratch.types.mark
    for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
        scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset])
    facts.raising-rules.append
        - RaisingRule(callee, given, result-type(types, local.answer, held), local.syntax)

────────────────────
_ do settle-forward
    - position Size

` Gives a member a union forwards the type its function answers with, where the call of a
` case lets errors out: those of every case that does, each once.
. forward = facts.forwards[position]
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. call = facts.first-call(forward.instance, forward.syntax)
while call != no-fact
    . fact = facts.calls[call]
    if fact.propagates && fact.callee != no-instance
        . signature = instances.signatures[fact.callee]
        for offset in 0 .. < signature.errors.count
            . error = instances.signature-types[signature.errors.start + offset]
            . known = false
            for held in mark .. < scratch.types.length
                if scratch.types[held] == error
                    known = true
            if !known
                scratch.types.push(error)
    call = fact.next
if scratch.types.length == mark || forward.value == invalid-type
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    =
. value = if forward.value == no-type then types.void-type else forward.value
facts.forwards[position].result = result-type(types, value, mark)

────────────────────
+ do release-typing

` Frees everything the type pass needed only while it ran: the facts, bindings, panic marks,
` relation memo, and the scratch stacks. Types and instances survive for emission, so
` the types must be sealed first.
if typing-released
    =
typing-released = true
panics.release()
facts.release()
facts-arena.release()
bindings.release()
relations.release()
scratch.release()

────────────────────
+ do release

if released
    =
released = true
release-typing()
instances.release()
types.release()
arena.release()

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do bound-types Types
    - program Program
    - scratch TypingScratch

. types = Types(program, scratch)
types.bind-types()
types.declare-unit-equalities()
= types
